(a) To encourage revitalization within the designated enterprise zone, the following exemptions schedule for state, county, and city ad valorem taxes are available to qualifying business and service enterprises:
(1) One hundred percent of the state, county and city ad valorem taxes shall be exempt for the first five years;
(2) Eighty percent of the state, county, and city ad valorem taxes shall be exempt for the next two years (sixth and seventh years);
(3) Sixty percent of the state, county, and city ad valorem taxes shall be exempt for the next year (eighth year);
(4) Forty percent of the state, city, and county ad valorem taxes shall be exempt for the next year (ninth year); and
(5) Twenty percent of the state, county, and city ad valorem taxes shall be exempt for the last year (tenth year).
(b) Pursuant to O.C.G.A. § 36-88-7(a)(1), the county board of commissioners and/or the Carrollton City Council may offer the following additional economic incentives if annually the board of commissioners and city council determine that such incentives are to be provided:
(1) Building permit fees;
(2) Sign permit fees;
(3) Business license fees;
(4) Rezoning fees;
(5) Engineering fees;
(6) Water and sewer tap fees;
(7) Other local fees authorized by the council and/or board.
(c) Nothing in this article shall authorize the county, Carrollton or their designated agents to waive, amend, provide exceptions to or otherwise modify or alter any ordinance that is expressly required to implement or enforce any statutory provisions or is designed to protect persons against discrimination on the basis of race, color, creed, national origin, sex, age, or handicap.
(d) For a qualifying business or service enterprise located within the enterprise zone or any business designated as eligible for enterprise zone advantages and incentives, the schedule provided for above shall begin in any year during which an area has an enterprise zone designation. Nothing contained in this article shall be construed as giving any business or service enterprise or property owner a vested right to be designated as a qualifying business or service enterprise.
(e) If, on or after the effective date of this article, a project within the designated enterprise zone consists of rehabilitation and improvement of an existing structure and the value of said improvements exceeds the value of the accompanying tract or parcel of land by a ratio of five to one (5:1), as determined by the county tax assessor or the Carrollton tax assessor, then the exemption schedule above shall also apply to the property whether or not the rehabilitation project is carried out by a qualifying business or service enterprise. The tax exemptions pursuant to this paragraph shall commence on the first day of the year following designation of the project as a qualifying project under this paragraph. However, this designation shall not be granted until the rehabilitation project has been completed and the county tax assessor or city tax assessor confirms its value.
(f) In no event shall the total value of the property tax exemptions granted within enterprise zones within the county and the city as a whole exceed ten percent of the value of the entire property tax digest of the county or the city.
(g) The enterprise zone designation shall run with the qualifying business or service enterprise and not with the land. Therefore, the designation shall apply only to the entity granted the designation through an application to the county and the city under this article.
(h) A business or service making application to receive enterprise zone tax exemptions and incentives shall have a right to appeal any denial of the application to the county board of commissioners and the city council. The request for appeal shall be filed with the director, the county attorney and the clerk of the county board of commissioners within seven days of the date of denial of the application for tax exemption. The county board of commissioners shall render a final decision on the appeal within 90 days of the filing of the appeal.
(Ord. of 9-3-02, § 1)

